		heading: `Where Paul was, and who he was writing to`,
		bodyHtml: `<p>Paul wrote Philippians while he was in chains, so &ldquo;worry about nothing&rdquo; does not come from a man with an easy life. The letter is full of thanks and joy to a church he cared for, and chapter 4 begins its closing advice with this: &ldquo;Rejoice in the Lord always; again I will say, rejoice.&rdquo; (Philippians 4:4).</p><p>The next line sets the tone for what follows: &ldquo;Show your gentleness to everyone. The Lord is near.&rdquo; (Philippians 4:5). Verses 6 and 7 are read best with that closeness in mind. The command not to worry rests on the fact that the Lord is near.`,
	},
