		id: 'worry',
		heading: `What “worry about nothing” asks`,
		bodyHtml: `<p>&ldquo;Worry about nothing; instead, in everything, through prayer and petition with thanksgiving, make your requests known to our Father.&rdquo; (Philippians 4:6). The verse does not stop at the prohibition. It gives a replacement: instead of carrying the worry, bring it.</p><p>It is not telling us to feel nothing, or to pretend a real problem is not real. It is telling us where to take the concern. Paul does not say a few things or the spiritual things. He says &ldquo;in everything.&rdquo; Nothing is too large or too small to be made known to our Father.`,
