		id: 'thanks',
		heading: `Why thanksgiving belongs in the prayer`,
		bodyHtml: `<p>The prayer is &ldquo;through prayer and petition with thanksgiving.&rdquo; (Philippians 4:6). Petition is asking. Thanksgiving is remembering what he has already done. Put together, they keep a request from turning into a complaint, because the one asking is also looking back at what our Father has given.</p><p>Paul himself prays like this from prison. He is not thankful because everything is fine. He is thankful because our Father is the one he is talking to.`,
	},
