		bodyHtml: `<p>&ldquo;The peace of our Father, beyond all understanding, will guard your hearts and your minds in Christ Jesus.&rdquo; (Philippians 4:7). Two details matter. First, this peace is <em>beyond all understanding</em>: it does not depend on the problem making sense or being solved. Second, it <em>guards</em> your hearts and minds, a picture of a sentry standing watch, so peace is described as something he provides to protect us, not something we must produce.</p><p>The verse does not say the request will be granted as asked. It says peace will come, and that it will be kept &ldquo;in Christ Jesus.&rdquo;`,
